STEPH­EN: He had three broth­ers, Gil­bert, Ed­mund, Richard. Gil­bert in his old age told some cava­liers he got a pass for nowt from Maister Gather­er one time mass he did and he seen his brud Maister Wull the play­writer up in Lun­non in a wrast­ling play wud a man on’s back. The play­house saus­age filled Gil­bert’s soul. He is nowhere: but an Ed­mund and a Richard are re­cor­ded in the works of sweet Wil­li­am.

