Bloom through the bardoor saw a shell held at their ears. He heard more faintly that that they heard, each for her­self alone, then each for oth­er, hear­ing the plash of waves, loudly, a si­lent roar.

Bronze by a weary gold, anear, afar, they listened.

Her ear too is a shell, the peep­ing lobe there. Been to the sea­side. Lovely sea­side girls. Skin tanned raw. Should have put on cold­cream first make it brown. Buttered toast. O and that lo­tion mustn’t for­get. Fever near her mouth. Your head it simply. Hair braided over: shell with sea­weed. Why do they hide their ears with sea­weed hair? And Turks the mouth, why? Her eyes over the sheet. Yash­mak. Find the way in. A cave. No ad­mit­tance ex­cept on busi­ness.

